35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The closeout files are revealing. Catalogue awards still serve users a decade later, while mechanism ones often stall.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The staffing rolls are alarming. Most phenotyping technicians left for industry. Modelling applicants are arriving, but the hands are gone.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The animal facility is accredited and has vet cover, but glasshouses are fully booked. Computing is free, yet animal day rates spiked.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The ledgers show vehicle costs frozen, but shipping is up. The repository migration is a genuine win, though.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,The incident logs show the spectroscopy suite was idle for eleven weeks. That is a major interruption risk for any project relying on it.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, that is a heavy burden. The hands are gone, but the minds remain. We must respect that gap.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, precisely. The minutes confirm the glasshouse crew is intact, but the modelling analysts are gone until autumn. We must pick accordingly.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Midori, that idle suite is critical. If a proposal depends on it, the schedule is already compromised before we start.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, that idle suite is a schedule killer. But my ledger data shows the bench-fee subsidy for glasshouses is still active. That is a real saving.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, yes. The station records confirm it. Three field sites lost a season to weather, while indoor rooms ran uninterrupted. We must avoid field-dependent work.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, the portfolio review confirms your worry. Live breeding causes double the overruns. We must avoid that fragility.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, that aligns with my findings. The technical hands are scarce. We must prioritize projects where the remaining staff can actually deliver the work.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, the free computing hours are a significant offset. We should favor simulation-heavy work to avoid the inflated animal unit costs.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, the free computing is a genuine offset. But the repository turnaround is now weeks, not months. That administrative burden has vanished for everyone.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that is good news. The administrative burden is gone, but the field risks remain. We must prioritize indoor work to avoid those weather delays.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I am glad the data is so clear. We should trust what has proven durable over time, rather than chasing novelty.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. The evidence points to stability. We must select a project that matches the staff we actually have, not the ones we lost.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. The infrastructure supports simulation and accredited animal work, but not field or spectroscopy. We must choose accordingly.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I am satisfied. The central costs are stable, and the administrative drag is gone. We can focus on the science now.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree. The data clearly favors indoor, stable work. We must avoid the field risks and broken equipment. Let us see the candidates.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
