60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I am looking at the candidates with a gentle eye. Candidate D, the Microbiome Atlas, feels like a catalogue. It matches the durable pattern we found.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate A relies on the glasshouse crew, which my minutes confirm is intact. That is the only option with verified human capacity.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Candidate C requires the idle spectroscopy suite. That is a critical failure point. I cannot support a proposal built on broken infrastructure.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate A benefits from the active bench-fee subsidy I found. That central coverage makes the greenhouse costs significantly lower than the headline suggests.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,Candidate D involves field collection across climate zones. My station records show those sites are high-risk for weather delays. I am concerned about the interruptions.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, that is a fair worry. But the closeout files show catalogue work endures. The field risk is real, yet the long-term value is proven.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, the catalogue value is real, but the field risk is immediate. We cannot rely on weather. I stand by Candidate A for its verified staffing.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, the glasshouse is booked solid through two cycles. Even with intact staff, the physical space is unavailable. Candidate A is a logistical dead end.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, the subsidy helps, but if the glasshouse is booked, the money is useless. Candidate C’s spectroscopy is also a dead end.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, that is a critical point. If the glasshouse is booked, Candidate A is stalled. I am leaning toward Candidate B, as indoor holding rooms ran uninterrupted in my records.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I understand your caution. Yet the closeout files show catalogue work endures. Candidate D’s long-term value is proven, even if the field work is risky.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, Candidate B requires the phenotyping technicians I found missing. Without those hands, the regeneration work cannot proceed. I cannot support it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, the animal facility is accredited with vet cover. The infrastructure is sound. The risk is purely staffing, which we must weigh against the other options.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, the staffing gap is real, but the central costs for B are stable. I am leaning toward B, as it avoids the broken equipment and field risks.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, that is a valid concern. But the indoor holding rooms were stable in my records. The risk is manageable, unlike the field or broken equipment.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I am ready to vote. The evidence points to stability and long-term utility. I trust the records over instinct.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I am ready to vote. The evidence is clear. We must choose the project that matches the staff we actually have, not the ones we lost.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
